Match the following physical constants in <strong>Column-I </strong>to their correct units given in <strong>Column-II</strong>:&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="width: 500px;"><tbody><tr><td></td><td style="text-align: center;"><strong>Column-I</strong></td><td></td><td style="text-align: center;"><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Column-II</strong></span></td></tr><tr><td>A.</td><td>Rate constant (k) of a second-order reaction</td><td>I.</td><td>m<sup>3</sup>mol<sup>-1</sup></td></tr><tr><td>B.</td><td>Cryoscopic constant (K<sub>f</sub>)</td><td>II.</td><td>mol<sup>-1</sup>L s<sup>-1</sup></td></tr><tr><td>C.</td><td>Van der Waals constant (b)</td><td>III.</td><td>No units</td></tr><tr><td>D.</td><td>Compressibility factor (Z)</td><td>IV.</td><td>kg K mol<sup>-1</sup></td></tr></tbody></table>
