<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td>Statement I:&nbsp;</td><td>The mass of a gas dissolved in a given mass of a solvent at any temperature is proportional to the pressure of the gas above the solvent.</td></tr><tr><td>Statement II:&nbsp;</td><td>The rate of dissolution of sugar is equal to the rate of crystallization of sugar at equilibrium.</td></tr></tbody></table>In light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td>1.&nbsp;</td><td>Both statement I and statement II are true.&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>2.&nbsp;</td><td>Both statement I and statement II are false.&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>3.&nbsp;</td><td>Statement I is true but statement II is false.&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>4.&nbsp;</td><td>Statement I is false but statement II is true.&nbsp;</td></tr></tbody></table>
